---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import RatingBadge from '../../components/RatingBadge.astro';
import { bySlug, monthRanges, destMonthUrl, type Destination } from '../../lib/data';

const slugs = ['aruba', 'puerto-rico', 'bahamas', 'turks-and-caicos', 'jamaica', 'punta-cana', 'cancun', 'miami', 'key-west', 'new-orleans', 'cabo-san-lucas', 'puerto-vallarta', 'cartagena'];
const rows = slugs.map((s) => bySlug.get(s)).filter((d): d is Destination => Boolean(d));
const peak = [7, 8, 9]; // Aug, Sep, Oct
---

<Guide slug="hurricane-season" photo="aruba">
  <p>
    The <strong>Atlantic hurricane season runs from 1 June to 30 November</strong>, and it covers the Caribbean, the Gulf of
    Mexico, Florida and Mexico's Yucatán coast (Cancún and the Riviera Maya). The Eastern Pacific season — which affects
    Mexico's Pacific resorts such as Los Cabos and Puerto Vallarta — starts a little earlier, on 15 May, and also ends on
    30 November.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most storms form between <strong>mid-August and mid-October</strong>, with the statistical peak around 10 September.
    June, July and November are far quieter. That doesn't mean you have to avoid the region for half the year — it means
    choosing your timing, your island and your booking terms carefully.
  </p>

  <h2>Hurricane risk by month</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>June–July:</b> early season; storms are possible but relatively uncommon. Expect heat, humidity and showers.</li>
    <li><b>August–October:</b> peak season. This is when the biggest and most frequent storms occur.</li>
    <li><b>November:</b> activity drops off quickly; by late November conditions are usually settled.</li>
    <li><b>December–May:</b> outside the season — the classic dry, sunny high season in the Caribbean.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How our destinations rate during peak season</h2>
  <p>
    Our weather scores already subtract points for August–October in hurricane-prone destinations. Here is how each one
    rates in the peak months, and when it's at its best:
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Destination</th><th scope="col">Aug</th><th scope="col">Sep</th><th scope="col">Oct</th><th scope="col">Best time</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map((d) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={d.url}>{d.name}</a></th>
              {peak.map((m) => (
                <td><a href={destMonthUrl(d, m)}><RatingBadge score={d.months[m].score} rating={d.months[m].rating} note={d.months[m].note} /></a></td>
              ))}
              <td class="left">{monthRanges(d.bestMonths)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>The safest places to go</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/destinations/aruba/">Aruba</a> and its neighbours Bonaire and Curaçao sit off the coast of Venezuela, south of
    the main hurricane belt, and are rarely hit. They're the best Caribbean bet if you must travel in September or October.
    Further afield, <a href="/destinations/cartagena/">Cartagena</a> on Colombia's Caribbean coast is also outside the usual
    storm track, though autumn is its rainy season.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have flexibility, the Pacific is a good alternative: <a href="/best-time-to-visit-hawaii/">Hawaii</a> is rarely
    affected by hurricanes and has some of its best weather in September and October.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips for travelling in hurricane season</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Buy travel insurance when you book</b> — policies bought after a storm is named usually won't cover it.</li>
    <li><b>Look for hurricane guarantees.</b> Many large resorts offer free rebooking or credit if a hurricane disrupts your stay.</li>
    <li><b>Book flexible fares and refundable rooms</b> so you can move dates if a storm threatens.</li>
    <li><b>Follow official forecasts</b> from the US National Hurricane Center, which tracks storms days in advance.</li>
    <li><b>Enjoy the upside:</b> fewer crowds and much lower prices, especially in June, July and November.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    See also: <a href="/guides/winter-sun/">winter sun destinations</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/warm-places-to-visit-in-december/">warm places to visit in December</a>.
  </p>
</Guide>

<style>
  td.left {
    text-align: left;
    white-space: normal;
  }
</style>
